 ## Change log
 
+- **2026-11-10, D131 Medigap intake stays in the conversation.** The owner rejects a duplicate form on the Medigap page. Show an invitation and “Talk to MidMorning” when pricing details are missing; open the existing conversation, reusing known reports and asking only for missing details with clear reasons and the existing answer buttons/free text. Do not send a message on the person’s behalf or consume an unsent draft. Profile corrections also return to chat. Complete profiles still show prices immediately; unknown/deferred answers, the 34101–34108/65–74 scope, 75+ unsupported message, privacy and source boundaries remain. No other tool changes. This refines D130’s presentation, not its capture or pricing rules. [Implementation and checks](audit-evidence/medigap-conversation-entry-20261110/README.md).
+
 - **2026-11-10, D130 Shared chat profile for Medigap pricing.** The owner requests automatically filling age, sex and tobacco status from the chat profile, updating prices when answers change, asking only for missing information, and adding clear profile questions with an explanation of why each detail is needed. Implement three local pricing meanings beside the unchanged 41-question inventory. Reuse exact age on November 10, 2026, including supported birthday arithmetic; never infer pricing sex from names/pronouns or a tobacco category from smoking history or silence. Keep beneficiary/helper scope, unknown/deferred/conflicting reports, corrections and existing sensitive-save/AI-context permissions. The existing Medigap tab automatically reads matched source prices for ZIPs 34101–34108 and ages 65–74; 75+ is unsupported. No other tool changes, new acquisition, paid model tests, source acceptance, ranking or hosted deployment are authorized. This supersedes D129’s separate visit-only lookup-input boundary only for these shared reported details; prices remain outside saved profiles/model context. [Implementation and verification](audit-evidence/medigap-chat-profile-20261110/README.md).
 
 - **2026-11-10, D129 Matched Medigap prices in the existing :8894 Plans UI.** The owner explicitly requests wiring the 34101–34108 cache into the app for immediate participant-matched Medigap prices, ages 65–74, with 75+ unsupported for this pilot. Reuse the MA cards/detail/comparison presentation in the existing Medigap tab. Keep Part D, the MA logic, conversation, protected apps and saved-data behavior unchanged. This authorizes the bounded local pilot display of exact source premiums, retaining the November 10, 2026 requested date, all classes, unknown qualifications and source STOPs; it is not authority for binding quotes, eligibility, recommendations, full-market completeness or hosted deployment. Keep the prior research build and its historical holds immutable; record this display scope separately. [Implementation and checks](audit-evidence/medigap-ui-8894-20261110/README.md).
